    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "body": "I have no benchmark, but I am about 99% sure that jax does not actually generate fused kernels for workloads involving e.g., matrix multiplications. For things like row-wise reductions (e.g., softmax), I can't speak for JAX but Triton is 4x faster than the PyTorch JIT. For sequences of element-wise operations, I would expect all existing JIT to do about just as well as Triton. Hope this answers your question.",
