    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "body": "I've given some explanations in the [softmax tutorial](https://triton-lang.org/getting-started/tutorials/02-fused-softmax.html#sphx-glr-getting-started-tutorials-02-fused-softmax-py). It seems like the torch.jit doesn't fuse anything at all, so it ends up being 4x slower than peak bandwidth (i.e. Triton) because it does 4x more memory transfers. Torch.native isn't very good either on V100 for these shapes, but I don't know why to be honest :)",
